@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — skip and delete unsubscribed addresses
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
box "Backend — Christian Fitness Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "PublishingClock" as clock
  participant "NewsletterUpkeep" as upkeep
end box
box "Backend — Christian Fitness Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "PurgeUnsubscribedHandler" as h
  participant "SendDueIssueHandler" as send
end box
box "Backend — Christian Fitness Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Christian Fitness database" as db
end box
== Every issue ==
send -> db : Recipients: Status = Subscribed and the kind switched on only
db --> send : No unsubscribed address (L2-058 AC6)
== Once a day ==
clock -> db : Take lease on TimeProvider tick
clock -> upkeep : Run daily job when due
upkeep -> h : Send PurgeUnsubscribedCommand
h -> db : Delete subscriptions UnsubscribedAt at least 29 days ago, so none outlives 30 days, with their confirmations
db --> h : Count deleted
h --> upkeep : Done; the log carries the count only
note over h : An address that subscribed again is Pending or Subscribed and is not deleted (L2-058 AC6)
@enduml
